   "answer": "The four types of reflection tokens used in SELF-RAG are:\n\n1. **Retrieve**: Decides when to retrieve with R [1].\n2. **ISREL**: Evaluates whether $d$ provides useful information to solve $x$ (with values {relevant, irrelevant}) [1].\n3. **ISSUP**: Evaluates whether all of the verification-worthy statements in $y$ are supported by $d$ (with values {fully supported, partially supported, no support}) [1].\n4. **ISUSE**: Evaluates whether $y$ is a useful response to $x$ (with values {5, 4, 3, 2, 1}) [1]. \n\nThe bottom three rows represent Critique tokens [1].",
